{
  "reasoning": "The organizer hint targets ambiguity around threshold_ratio behavior and its tuning interactions. The current doc already states the predicate and monotonicity, but it lacks a dedicated, fully explicit section that ties tuning to window_size/min_duration/start_time and includes practical cautions aligned to the video-silence-remover task (opening skip + long pauses) and avoids any contradictory phrasing. I will (1) replace the threshold-ratio parameter bullet with a more explicit, monotonic definition and interaction notes, (2) insert a focused Threshold ratio section under Parameters Tuning with concrete starting ranges and task-aligned advice, (3) fix the incorrect note about inclusive min_duration (it’s min_duration, not threshold, and inclusive wording may be wrong/unclear), and (4) strengthen the start-time note to match “start after opening boundary”.",
  "edits": [
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "target": "- `--threshold-ratio`: Low-energy cutoff as a fraction of the **local average** (default: 0.5). A second is marked “pause/low energy” when `energy < local_avg × threshold_ratio`. **Higher values** mark more seconds as pauses (more aggressive removal). **Lower values** are stricter and mark fewer pauses.",
      "content": "- `--threshold-ratio`: Low-energy cutoff **multiplier** relative to the local average (default: 0.5).\n  - **Exact condition:** a second is marked low-energy when `energy < (local_avg * threshold_ratio)`.\n  - **Monotonic behavior:** increasing `threshold_ratio` raises the cutoff, so **more** seconds satisfy the inequality (more aggressive pause detection / removal). Decreasing it lowers the cutoff, so **fewer** seconds are flagged (stricter; preserves more content).\n  - Interactions: `local_avg` depends on `--window-size`; use `--min-duration` to suppress brief dips; use `--start-time` to ignore the opening/intro boundary before tuning the ratio."
    },
    {
      "op": "insert_after",
      "target": "## Parameters Tuning",
      "content": "\n\n### `threshold_ratio` (most important knob)\n\nThe detector flags low-energy seconds using `energy < (local_avg * threshold_ratio)`. Because the predicate is strict `<`, **higher `threshold_ratio` always produces the same-or-more low-energy seconds** (never fewer).\n\n**Task-aligned tuning (teaching videos):**\n- Start at **0.4–0.6** (often `0.5`).\n- If long board-writing silences are **not** being removed, increase gradually (e.g., `0.5 → 0.6 → 0.65`).\n- If quiet speech is being removed (soft voice, distant mic, writing while speaking), decrease (e.g., `0.5 → 0.45 → 0.4`).\n- Pair with `--min-duration >= 2` to target “real” pauses and avoid cutting natural micro-pauses.\n\n**Interactions / gotchas:**\n- `--window-size`: larger windows make `local_avg` smoother (often fewer rapid on/off toggles); smaller windows track quick loudness changes and can over-trigger in dynamic speech.\n- `--start-time`: set this to **just after the opening** (static/noise intro) so the local average is computed on teaching content; otherwise the intro can skew early thresholds."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "target": "- Use --start-time to skip detected opening",
      "content": "- Use `--start-time` to begin analysis **just after** the opening/intro boundary (so the local average and detected pauses reflect teaching content)."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "target": "- Preserve pauses whose duration equals `--min-duration`; the threshold is inclusive",
      "content": "- `--min-duration` controls filtering of detected low-energy runs; if you see too many short “blips,” increase `--min-duration` (e.g., 2 → 3)."
    }
  ]
}

